1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
Are you ready to play a game?

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:04,760
It is called Beat the Beads!

3
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:08,680
I will spin the wheel, and it will land on a number.

4
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:13,040
You tell me that number's friend, before I count to three.

5
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:17,880
If the beads get stuck, you will know exactly what to do.

6
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:20,980
Let's find out who remembers best.

7
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:25,160
Round one — spin the wheel!

8
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:29,560
It lands on add one.

9
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:33,420
Make four, then try to add one more.

10
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:36,460
Look at that, we are stuck.

11
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:39,380
Quick — what is one's friend?

12
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,300
One's friend is four!

13
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,520
Four plus one is five!

14
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,580
Round two — spin the wheel!

15
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:54,860
It lands on take away three.

16
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:58,860
Make six, then try to take away three.

17
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:02,240
Uh oh, we are stuck again.

18
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:05,960
Think fast — what is three's friend?

19
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:09,280
Three's friend is two!

20
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:12,760
Six take away three is three!

21
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:17,180
Round three — spin the wheel!

22
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:21,320
It lands on add four.

23
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:25,440
Make one, then try to add four more.

24
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:27,520
Stuck already?

25
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,560
Let's fix that.

26
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:33,520
Here it comes — what is four's friend?

27
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,260
Four's friend is one!

28
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:40,700
One plus four is five!

29
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:45,320
Round four — spin the wheel!

30
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:49,880
It lands on take away two.

31
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:54,060
Make six, then try to take away two.

32
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:58,060
There it is — stuck once more.

33
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:00,060
Can you get this one?

34
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,460
What is two's friend?

35
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:06,100
Two's friend is three!

36
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:09,500
Six take away two is four!

37
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:15,560
Four down, four to go — you are on fire today!

38
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:19,160
If you are having fun, tap that like button.

39
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:24,440
The wheel keeps mixing it up — you never know what is coming next!

40
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:28,880
Round five — spin the wheel!

41
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:33,200
It lands on take away one.

42
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:37,280
Make five, then try to take away one.

43
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:42,360
We are stuck, but we know exactly what to do.

44
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:46,540
You know this one — what is one's friend?

45
00:02:48,380 --> 00:02:50,200
One's friend is four!

46
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,620
Five take away one is four!

47
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:58,040
Round six — spin the wheel!

48
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:02,120
It lands on add three.

49
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:06,440
Make two, then try to add three more.

50
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:08,400
Stuck!

51
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:11,600
Lucky for us, we have a trick.

52
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:13,980
What is three's friend?

53
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:15,480
Tell me!

54
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,380
Three's friend is two!

55
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:21,960
Two plus three is five!

56
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,380
Round seven — spin the wheel!

57
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:30,860
It lands on take away four.

58
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:35,280
Make seven, then try to take away four.

59
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,920
Here we go again — stuck!

60
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:43,360
You know this one too — what is four's friend?

61
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:46,840
Four's friend is one!

62
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,460
Seven take away four is three!

63
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:54,980
Round eight — spin the wheel!

64
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:59,000
It lands on add two.

65
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,080
Make three, then try to add two more.

66
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:06,660
One more stuck moment to solve.

67
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:10,600
Last one — what is two's friend?

68
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:13,920
Two's friend is three!

69
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,060
Three plus two is five!

70
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:21,280
You just beat all eight small friends!

71
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,900
Four for adding, and four for taking away.

72
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:28,500
That is every small friend there is.

73
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:32,200
Try Beat the Beads on your own abacus at home.

74
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:38,980
For more sums to practice, search for Abacus Kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

75
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:40,660
Download it free.

76
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:47,860
Next time, we will meet a brand new kind of friend — the Big Friends of ten.

77
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:49,880
See you next time!
